      "text": "We start with the given equation:\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}\\right) = 12.\n\\]\nLet \\( y = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} \\). Then the equation becomes:\n\\[\ny^2 + y = 12.\n\\]\nWe can rewrite this as a standard quadratic equation:\n\\[\ny^2 + y - 12 = 0.\n\\]\nNext, we solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\( y = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\), where \\( a = 1 \\), \\( b = 1 \\), and \\( c = -12 \\). Plugging in these values, we get:\n\\[\ny = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot (-12)}}{2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1 + 48}}{2} = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} = \\frac{-1 \\pm 7}{2}.\n\\]\nThis gives us two solutions for \\( y \\):\n\\[\ny = \\frac{-1 + 7}{2} = \\frac{6}{2} = 3,\n\\]\nand\n\\[\ny = \\frac{-1 - 7}{2} = \\frac{-8}{2} = -4.\n\\]\nNow, we need to solve for \\( x \\) in the equations \\( \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = 3 \\) and \\( \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = -4 \\).\n\nFirst, consider \\( \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = 3 \\):\n\\[\n4x - 16 = 3(3x - 4).\n\\]\nExpanding and simplifying, we get:\n\\[\n4x - 16 = 9x - 12,\n\\]\n\\[\n-16 + 12 = 9x - 4x,\n\\]\n\\[\n-4 = 5x,\n\\]\n\\[\nx = -\\frac{4}{5}.\n\\]\n\nNext, consider \\( \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = -4 \\):\n\\[\n4x - 16 = -4(3x - 4).\n\\]\nExpanding and simplifying, we get:\n\\[\n4x - 16 = -12x + 16,\n\\]\n\\[\n4x + 12x = 16 + 16,\n\\]\n\\[\n16x = 32,\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 2.\n\\]\n\nThe greatest possible value of \\( x \\) is \\( 2 \\). Therefore, the answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}.\n\\]",
